.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH cursor-session-show 1 "" "cursor-session 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cursor\-session\-show \- Show messages from a session
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcursor\-session show\fR [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-short\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISESSION_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show messages from a session
.PP
The header\*(Aqs `tokens:` line (`token_estimate` in \-\-json) estimates how many tokens the messages `show` prints by default take: ceil(characters / 4). Tool calls and results are not counted. It is an estimate, not any model\*(Aqs tokenizer count.
.PP
The header\*(Aqs `messages:` and `tokens:` lines (`message_count` and `token_estimate` in \-\-json) are always those of the whole session, whatever \-\-only, \-\-short or \-\-limit print.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
Only read this store; the other one is never opened
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
agent: Cursor Agent CLI chats (~/.cursor/chats and agent transcripts)
.IP \(bu 2
ide: Cursor IDE composer chats (state.vscdb)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<N>\fR
Print only the last N messages [default: 20 in a terminal, all when piped or with \-\-json]
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Print the full transcript
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<ROLES>\fR
Print only messages of these roles, comma\-separated; `tool` adds the tool calls and results, which are left out otherwise, a call that failed or was stopped marked `(error)` or `(cancelled)`. \-\-limit counts only the messages printed
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
user: What the user wrote
.IP \(bu 2
assistant: The model\*(Aqs replies
.IP \(bu 2
tool: Tool calls and their results
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-short\fR
Cut each message to its first 300 characters, and tool calls and results to a one\-line preview
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the session and its messages as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISESSION_ID\fR>
Session ID, or a unique prefix of one (case\-insensitive)
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read only this location: a home, .cursor, chats, workspace, session or projects directory, a store.db or state.vscdb file, or the directory that holds state.vscdb
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the storage paths in use and the rows and files that were skipped to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
cursor\-session show f4eea6d2
cursor\-session show f4eea6d2 \-\-all
cursor\-session show f4eea6d2 \-\-json \-\-limit 5
cursor\-session show f4eea6d2 \-\-only user,assistant \-\-short
cursor\-session show f4eea6d2 \-\-only tool \-\-limit 10
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.RS 4
.nf
0  Success, also when output is cut short by a closed pipe (e.g. `| head`)
1  Error: session not found, no sessions match (search), unreadable storage, failed healthcheck
2  Usage error: unknown command or flag, invalid value
.fi
.RE
